</section>

<!-- S6b — TWO WORDS -->
<section class="s-twowords ir">
  <div class="ic">
    <div class="twowords-box">
      <h3>Two words we chose carefully</h3>
      <p><strong>No action</strong> is not <em>discard</em>. Nothing is deleted; the excerpt stays visible on the document.</p>
      <p><strong>Dismiss</strong> takes it off <em>my</em> Huddle. It stays on the shared chart timeline — because the timeline is the record, and one clinician’s triage isn’t a chart decision.</p>
      <p>A personal view choice and a shared clinical decision are different things, and the interface never lets them blur.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- S6c — FRESHNESS -->
<section class="s-freshness ir">
  <div class="ic">
    <p class="freshness-note">And they get out of the way on their own. Content past a freshness window, or predating your own last signed encounter, drops off the at-a-glance view — it’s already been accounted for. Anything still pending never goes stale.</p>
