    <div class="guarantee-inner">
      <div class="il">THE GUARANTEE</div>
      <h2>Outside records inform the clinician. They never write the clinician’s note.</h2>
      <p>This isn’t a policy, it’s an architecture. The code that reads excerpts is physically separate from the code that drafts notes, and an automated test fails the build if the note-generating path so much as imports the excerpt reader.</p>
      <p>The only way outside content enters a note is one explicit click — <strong>Include in note</strong> — which inserts it as an attributed quote:</p>
      <p class="guarantee-quote">Per Discharge Summary, Dr. A. Chen, 3/15/24: “…”</p>
      <p class="guarantee-close">Your record stays your record. And where it isn’t, it says so on the page.</p>
