        <h2>Ten phone calls, and we make them.</h2>
        <p>You don’t port a number and you don’t switch anything off. You get a Stream fax number, your old line keeps working, and there’s no moment where a fax could fall between two systems.</p>
        <p>Then we make the calls. Most practices find that ten senders — the hospital records department, the specialty groups they refer to most, the imaging center — account for the majority of what comes in. We contact them with your new number as part of setup, so most of your inbound volume is running through Stream the same week without anyone at your front desk picking up the phone.</p>
        <p>Everything else moves at its own pace. And whatever still arrives the old way, or on paper, gets dragged into Stream from the Documents page and goes down the same pipeline.</p>
